lations to ensure precision. The key is understanding how the second difference operator D is constructed and how it transforms the matrix for the HP filter calculation.\n\nThe row structures for D show a systematic pattern of differences between adjacent elements, creating a (n-2) x n matrix that captures the second-order changes in the sequence.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_04dd1d073c864b0e8135d52a","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Explore available treasury bulletin resources to find receipt/outlay data\n- [x] Extract nominal total receipts and total outlays for FY 2010-2024\n- [x] Apply Hodrick-Prescott filter (lambda=100) to receipts series\n- [x] Apply Hodrick-Prescott filter (lambda=100) to outlays series\n- [x] Compute structural balance (trend receipts - trend outlays) for each year\n- [x] Compute actual balance (receipts - outlays) for each year\n- [x] For FY 2024: report actual balance, structural balance, and absolute gap\n- [x] Round to nearest whole number (millions), format as [val1, val2, val3]\n- [x] Write answer to /app/answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
